  "driver": "STM32N6 universal synchronous/asynchronous receiver transmitter (USART1) UART hardware abstraction layer (HAL) driver as delivered by ST (STM32CubeN6 v1.4.0)",
  "target": {
    "part_number": "STM32N657X0 (STM32N6x5/x7 family)",
    "core": "Arm Cortex-M55",
    "silicon_revision": "UNSPECIFIED",
    "source_documents": [
      "DS14791 Rev 9",
      "RM0486 Rev 4 chapter 65 (USART) + memory map p.180"
    ],
    "hsi_contract": "RM0486 Rev 4 ch.65 USART register interface + memory map p.180 (USART1 secure base 0x52001000)",
    "safety_allocation": "NOT_PROVIDED: no owner safety scope recorded for the USART benchmark work orders"
  },
  "scope": [
    "HAL (classic, handle-based) as delivered by ST: UART_HandleTypeDef with its Instance (the CMSIS device structure USART1, stm32n6xx.h) and Init configuration; HAL_StatusTypeDef results; the HAL framework headers and ST's stm32n6xx_hal_conf_template.h configured with the UART module, the DMA module headers the handle type needs and the RCC module headers for the kernel clock (USE_FULL_ASSERT off, as delivered); the kernel clock frequency comes from HAL_RCCEx_GetPeriphCLKFreq (RCC HAL, not delivered: the test environment provides it, 64 MHz)",
    "Initialisation and de-initialisation from the handle configuration (baud rate, word length, stop bits, parity, mode TX/RX, oversampling, one-bit sampling, kernel clock prescaler; USART_CR1, USART_CR2, USART_CR3, USART_BRR, USART_PRESC), FIFO disabled; blocking transmit and receive of a buffer with a timeout in ms of the HAL time base HAL_GetTick (USART_TDR, USART_RDR, USART_ISR TXE/RXNE/TC/TEACK/REACK); the handle state and error code",
    "Out of scope: the MSP hooks (weak, empty as delivered), interrupt and DMA transfers (and the abort functions, which use the DMA module), half-duplex, LIN, multiprocessor, receiver timeout, auto baud rate, RS-485 and smartcard/IrDA modes, the FIFO, hardware flow control, the extended API, register callbacks"
  ],
  "system_names": [
    "USART HAL driver",
    "USART driver",
    "STM32N6 USART HAL driver"
  ],
